  "steps": [
    "Mix besan, salt, pepper and yogurt along with 1/3rd cup water or slightly more to make a smooth batter like dosa (slightly thinner)",
    "On a pan add some butter, spread onions and spinach onto it.",
    "After 2-3 mins, add your besan batter (thin layer not thick) onto the spinach and onion base and cover wnd cook for 5-6 mins on low-med flame.",
    "Add oregano, chilli flakes, pepper, paneer and shredded cheese. Press down well with the flap so it sticks onto the cheela.",
    "Cover again and cook for another 7-8 mins until you can see that the bottom is well caramalized nothing is wet on the top portion.",
    "No need to flip and cook. Just fold it, cut into halves and enjoy with your fav chutney/sauce."
